<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Mini Player play/pause press feedback.

  It replaces `?attr/selectableItemBackgroundBorderless`, which is what produced
  the oversized, cropped circle the brief describes. Two things go wrong with a
  borderless ripple here and they compound:

    1. It is unbounded, so its radius comes from the view's larger dimension -
       the control's box is 27x48, so the circle is drawn about 48 across on a
       27-wide control and immediately spills out of it.
    2. Being borderless it projects onto the nearest ancestor that has a
       background, and that ancestor is the pill itself (`bg_mini_player`). So
       the spill is not drawn against the button at all - it is drawn across the
       pill and then cut by the pill's own rounded outline, which is the crop.

  A ripple with a mask is bounded: it cannot project past the view it is on, and
  it is clipped to the mask rather than to whatever is behind it.

  **The mask is a circle - G4a.** It used to be the full 27x48 hit area with its
  corners taken to half the width, which is a vertical stadium: 27 across and 48
  tall, so the pressed and focused state drew a stretched oval around a round
  control. The frozen control is round - `Button` 27x25 r9999 on the HOME pill,
  `Mini-player / play` 48x48 r24 in the kit - so the ink is now a true 27dp
  circle, the full width of the slot, inset top and bottom to sit centred on the
  glyph. The slot, the 27x48 hit target and the control's position are all
  unchanged: the touch still lands anywhere in the slot, only the drawn press
  shape is round.

  `colorControlHighlight` is the theme's own press colour, so Light and Dark are
  both the platform's and neither needs a value here.
-->
<ripple xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:color="?attr/colorControlHighlight">

    <item android:id="@android:id/mask">
        <inset
            android:insetTop="@dimen/mini_player_control_press_inset"
            android:insetBottom="@dimen/mini_player_control_press_inset">
            <shape android:shape="oval">
                <solid android:color="@android:color/white" />
            </shape>
        </inset>
    </item>
</ripple>
